<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Baluchistan States Union</h1><p class="st-meta">1952 CE – 1955 CE · capital Kalat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived federation of the four princely states of Balochistan within Pakistan, led by the Khan of Kalat.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1952 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Kalat</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kharan-state">Kharan</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/makran-state">Makran State</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/las-bela-state">Las Bela State</a>, which had acceded to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1948, were combined into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Baluchistan</a> States Union. The Khan of Kalat, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-yar-khan">Ahmad Yar Khan</a>, became its head as Khan-e-Azam.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The union had a council of the rulers and a small administration based at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Kalat</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan's</a> government retaining control of defence, foreign affairs and communications. It covered a vast, thinly populated territory of pastoralists, farmers and coastal fishermen.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1955 the union was dissolved and merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> under the One Unit scheme, ending the political role of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch-people">Baloch</a> rulers. Its lands are now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a> province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/baluchistan-states-union.jpg" alt="Baluchistan States Union" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: WikiCobalt-Chloride- · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FlagofKalat.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1952 CE – 1955 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalat</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmad Yar Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Balochi, Brahui</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Balochistan States Union</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1954&amp;focus=baluchistan-states-union" aria-label="Baluchistan States Union on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6418 1116 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Baluchistan States Union lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6738 1372L6778 1519M6738 1372L6738 1372M6738 1372L6751 1470M6738 1372L6710 1388M6738 1372L6666 1478"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6778 1519h0M6738 1372h0M6751 1470h0M6710 1388h0M6666 1478h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6738 1372h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6738 1372h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kalat. <a href="/atlas?year=1954&amp;focus=baluchistan-states-union">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
